---
description: SEO and structured data rules
alwaysApply: true
---

- Use the Next.js Metadata API (`generateMetadata` / the `metadata` export) for title,
  description, Open Graph, and Twitter card tags — never manually inject `<head>` tags.
- All metadata content (clinic name, description, address) must pull from `siteData`,
  not be re-typed as separate hardcoded strings.
- Include `LocalBusiness`/`Dentist` JSON-LD structured data in the root layout, built
  from `siteData` (name, address, phone, hours, geo coordinates if available). Include
  `FAQPage` JSON-LD generated from `siteData.faqs` on the FAQ section.
- Generate `sitemap.xml` and `robots.txt` using Next.js's `app/sitemap.ts` and
  `app/robots.ts` conventions — not static files.
- Every page/section needs exactly one `<h1>`; don't duplicate `<h1>` across sections.
- Verify metadata renders server-side (view page source, not just dev tools' rendered
  DOM) before considering an SEO phase complete.
- Favicon and social share preview image (Open Graph image) must use the clinic's real
  logo/branding, sourced via `siteData.clinic.logoPath`, once available — not a generic
  Next.js/Vercel default icon.
